# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intermediate extracts -- DELIBERATELY NOT PUBLISHED.
#
# These four files are the full parse of the division's PDF, and they still
# contain the two fields build_corpus.py excludes from the public corpus on
# editorial grounds:
#
#   email_q         108 non-blank. The field that solicited contact details;
#                   its redactions leave location-identifying gaps
#                   ("we are planning to move from .").
#   employee_where  1 non-blank, and it names an individual staff member's
#                   school.
#
# Both are technically inside the division's own published PDF, but committing
# them here would turn "buried in 3,106 pages" into "grep-able JSON," which is
# a different thing in practice and reverses a decision that was made on
# purpose. Anyone can regenerate all four from the source PDF -- see README.md
# -- so nothing reproducible is lost by keeping them out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
survey_raw.txt
survey_clean.txt
records.json
records_clean.json

# The source PDF, 9.3 MB. Excluded by default: the division publishes it, and
# git history is forever. See README.md if you decide to archive it here.
Redacted-Redistricting-Survey-Raw-Results-Final-June-2026.pdf

# Generated: the artifact build, with the whole corpus inlined. Rebuild with
# build_site.py. docs/ IS committed -- GitHub Pages serves it.
site/explorer.build.html

# Local tooling
.claude/settings.local.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Serena tool scratch (matches wjcc/omnomnom/trivia)
.serena/

# Bash-sandbox bind-mount artifacts. The sandbox masks a list of dotfiles by
# bind-mounting /dev/null over them inside the project root, which leaves them
# here as zero-byte character special files -- not real config, just mount
# points. They are recreated on every sandboxed command and only clutter
# `git status`. Confirm with `stat -c %F <file>`: "character special file"
# means artifact, "regular file" means someone actually put config there.
.bashrc
.bash_profile
.zshrc
.zprofile
.profile
.gitconfig
.gitmodules
.ripgreprc
.idea
.vscode
.mcp.json

# Screencasts and their GIF conversions. Recorded locally for the devlog /
# Substack posts; the published copies live in the post, not in git history.
*.mp4
*.gif
